module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.Generators

/-!
# Iterated cones in the subcategory generated by an object

Let `D` be a triangulated category. This file proves the one abstract statement that the
generation arguments which run over a bounded resolution end with:

> Let `Y 0 ⟶ Y 1 ⟶ ⋯ ⟶ Y N` be a finite tower in which each step sits in a distinguished
> triangle `Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦1⟧`. If `Y 0` and all the `B i` lie in a strictly
> full subcategory closed under extensions, then so does `Y N`.

This is the Postnikov tower on the stupid filtration of a complex, read in the triangulated
category. If `0 ⟶ A 0 ⟶ A 1 ⟶ ⋯ ⟶ A M ⟶ 0` is an acyclic complex and `U p` denotes the stupid
truncation `σ^{≤p}` of it, then `U M` is the whole (acyclic, hence zero) complex, `U 0` is the
initial term `A 0`, and the stupid filtration gives distinguished triangles
`U p ⟶ U (p - 1) ⟶ (A p)⟦1 - p⟧ ⟶ (U p)⟦1⟧`. Taking `Y i := U (M - i)` and
`B i := (A (M - i))⟦1 - (M - i)⟧` puts these into the shape above, with `Y 0 = U M` zero; the
conclusion `Y M = A 0` is the statement that the initial term of a bounded acyclic complex lies
in any shift-stable, extension-closed subcategory containing the other terms.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_triangleChain` — the tower statement itself, for any
  property of objects closed under isomorphisms and under extensions
  (`ObjectProperty.IsTriangulatedClosed₂`). No shift stability is used.
* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_triangleChain` — the same with `Y 0` only
  assumed to be a zero object, which is how an acyclic complex enters.
* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration` — the same again, indexed
  the way the stupid filtration of a bounded acyclic complex produces it, so that the
  conclusion is about the initial term of the complex.
* `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.genProp` and the instances
  `ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderRetracts`, `ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderShift ℤ` and
  `ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated` on it — the subcategory `⟨E⟩` of [Stacks, Tag 09SI] is a
  triangulated subcategory closed under retracts and shifts.
* `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.mem_gen_of_triangleChain`,
  `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.mem_gen_of_isZero_triangleChain` and
  `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.mem_gen_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration` — the tower statement
  for `⟨E⟩`, in the three indexings.
* `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.mem_smd_iff_exists_retract` — in a pretriangulated category an
  object is a direct summand of an object of `A` exactly when it is a retract of one.

## Implementation notes

The subcategories `⟨E⟩ₙ`, namely `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.genN`, are built from `smd`,
`add` and `⋆` as sets of objects, whereas Mathlib's triangulated-subcategory API is stated for
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty` and uses `ObjectProperty.retractClosure` and
`ObjectProperty.extensionProduct`. The two match up: `smd A` is the retract closure of `A`
(`mem_smd_iff_exists_retract`; a retract of an object `Z` of a pretriangulated category is a
direct summand of `Z`, because the triangle on a split mono splits) and `A ⋆ B` is
`ObjectProperty.extensionProduct A B` on the nose, since the latter is already closed under
isomorphisms. The private lemma `genN_eq_retractClosure_extensionProductIter` records the
resulting identification
`⟨E⟩ₙ = ((add (shiftCat E)).extensionProductIter n).retractClosure`,
which is what lets the closure properties of `⟨E⟩` be read off from Mathlib — in particular
associativity of `⋆`, i.e. [Stacks, Tag 0FX1], is not reproved here.

`⟨E⟩` is not identified with `(ObjectProperty.singleton E).triangEnvelope`, although it is equal
to it: that would additionally need `add (shiftCat E)` and
`((singleton E).shiftClosure ℤ).binaryProductsClosure` to have the same retract closure, which
is not needed for anything below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09SI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09SI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FX0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FX0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FX1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FX1)
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated

namespace CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

/-! ### Retract closures and shifts -/

section RetractShift

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] {A : Type*} [AddMonoid A] [HasShift C A]
  (P : ObjectProperty C)

/-- The retract closure of a property stable under the shift by `a` is stable under the shift
by `a`: the shift functor carries a retract `X ⟶ Z ⟶ X` to a retract
`X⟦a⟧ ⟶ Z⟦a⟧ ⟶ X⟦a⟧`. -/
instance isStableUnderShiftBy_retractClosure (a : A) [P.IsStableUnderShiftBy a] :
    P.retractClosure.IsStableUnderShiftBy a where
  le_shift := by
    rintro X ⟨Z, hZ, ⟨r⟩⟩
    exact ⟨(shiftFunctor C a).obj Z, P.le_shift a _ hZ, ⟨r.map (shiftFunctor C a)⟩⟩

/-- The retract closure of a property stable under all shifts by `A` is stable under all shifts
by `A`. -/
instance isStableUnderShift_retractClosure [P.IsStableUnderShift A] :
    P.retractClosure.IsStableUnderShift A where

end RetractShift

/-! ### Iterated cones -/

section IteratedCone

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ] [Preadditive C]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]

/-- **A finite tower of extensions of objects of `P` lies in `P`.** Let `P` be a property of
objects of a pretriangulated category which is closed under isomorphisms and under extensions,
and let `Y : ℕ → C`, `B : ℕ → C` be such that for every `i < N` there is a distinguished
triangle `Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦1⟧`. If `Y 0` and every `B i` with `i < N` satisfy
`P`, then so does `Y N`.

This is the Postnikov tower on the stupid filtration of a bounded complex: each step adds one
term `B i` of the complex to the truncation computed so far. -/
theorem prop_of_triangleChain (P : ObjectProperty C) [P.IsTriangulatedClosed₂]
    [P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] {Y B : ℕ → C} (N : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ i < N, ∃ (f : Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1)) (g : Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i) (h : B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang C)
    (hY : P (Y 0)) (hB : ∀ i < N, P (B i)) : P (Y N) := by
  induction N with
  | zero => exact hY
  | succ n ih =>
    have hn : P (Y n) := ih (fun i hi => hT i (by omega)) fun i hi => hB i (by omega)
    obtain ⟨f, g, h, hd⟩ := hT n (by omega)
    exact P.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₂ (Triangle.mk f g h) hd hn (hB n (by omega))

/-- **The initial term of a bounded acyclic complex.** The tower statement
`ObjectProperty.prop_of_triangleChain` in the form in which an acyclic complex supplies it: the
bottom of the tower is only assumed to be a zero object, which is what the stupid truncation
`σ^{≤M}` of an acyclic complex concentrated in degrees `0, …, M` is. -/
theorem prop_of_isZero_triangleChain (P : ObjectProperty C) [P.IsTriangulatedClosed₂]
    [P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [P.ContainsZero] {Y B : ℕ → C} (N : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ i < N, ∃ (f : Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1)) (g : Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i) (h : B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang C)
    (hY : IsZero (Y 0)) (hB : ∀ i < N, P (B i)) : P (Y N) :=
  P.prop_of_triangleChain N hT (P.prop_of_iso ((isZero_zero C).iso hY) P.prop_zero) hB

/-- **The initial term of a bounded acyclic complex lies in `P`.** This is
`ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_triangleChain` with the tower indexed the way the stupid
filtration of a complex produces it. Let `0 ⟶ A 0 ⟶ ⋯ ⟶ A M ⟶ 0` be a complex concentrated in
degrees `0, …, M` in an abelian category with derived category `C`, let `U p` be its stupid
truncation `σ^{≤p}`, so that `U 0 = A 0` and `U M` is the whole complex, and let `B p` be the
shift `(A p)⟦1 - p⟧`; the stupid filtration supplies distinguished triangles
`U p ⟶ U (p - 1) ⟶ B p ⟶ (U p)⟦1⟧` for `1 ≤ p ≤ M`. If the complex is acyclic then `U M` is a
zero object, and the conclusion `P (U 0)` says that the initial term `A 0` lies in `P` as soon
as `B 1, …, B M` do. -/
theorem prop_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration (P : ObjectProperty C) [P.IsTriangulatedClosed₂]
    [P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [P.ContainsZero] {U B : ℕ → C} (M : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ p, 0 < p → p ≤ M → ∃ (f : U p ⟶ U (p - 1)) (g : U (p - 1) ⟶ B p)
      (h : B p ⟶ (U p)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧), Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang C)
    (hU : IsZero (U M)) (hB : ∀ p, 0 < p → p ≤ M → P (B p)) : P (U 0) := by
  simpa using P.prop_of_isZero_triangleChain (Y := fun i => U (M - i)) (B := fun i => B (M - i)) M
    (fun i hi => hT (M - i) (by omega) (by omega)) hU fun i hi => hB (M - i) (by omega) (by omega)

end IteratedCone

end CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

namespace Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators

variable {D : Type*} [Category D] [Preadditive D] [HasShift D ℤ] [HasZeroObject D]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] [IsTriangulated D]
  [HasFiniteBiproducts D]

/-! ### Direct summands are retracts -/

omit [IsTriangulated D] [HasFiniteBiproducts D] in
/-- **A direct summand of an object of `A` is the same thing as a retract of one.** The
nontrivial direction is that a retract splits off: if `X ⟶ Z ⟶ X` is the identity then `X ⟶ Z`
is a split mono, so the third map of a distinguished triangle `X ⟶ Z ⟶ W ⟶ X⟦1⟧` vanishes and
the triangle exhibits `Z ≅ X ⊞ W`. -/
theorem mem_smd_iff_exists_retract {A : Set D} {X : D} :
    X ∈ smd A ↔ ∃ Z ∈ A, Nonempty (Retract X Z) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨Z, Y, hZ, ⟨e⟩⟩
    refine ⟨Z, hZ, ⟨⟨biprod.inl ≫ e.inv, e.hom ≫ biprod.fst, ?_⟩⟩⟩
    rw [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, biprod.inl_fst]
  · rintro ⟨Z, hZ, ⟨r⟩⟩
    obtain ⟨W, g, h, hd⟩ := distinguished_cocone_triangle r.i
    have hsm : IsSplitMono r.i := ⟨⟨r.r, r.retract⟩⟩
    obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := exists_iso_binaryBiproduct_of_distTriang _ hd
      (Triangle.mor₃_eq_zero_of_mono₁ _ hd (by dsimp; infer_instance))
    exact ⟨Z, W, hZ, ⟨e⟩⟩

omit [IsTriangulated D] [HasFiniteBiproducts D] in
private theorem retractClosure_eq_smd (A : Set D) :
    ObjectProperty.retractClosure (fun X => X ∈ A) = fun X => X ∈ smd A := by
  ext X
  rw [ObjectProperty.prop_retractClosure_iff, mem_smd_iff_exists_retract]
  simp

omit [IsTriangulated D] [HasFiniteBiproducts D] in
private theorem extensionProduct_eq_star (A B : Set D) :
    ObjectProperty.extensionProduct (fun X => X ∈ A) (fun X => X ∈ B) =
      fun X => X ∈ starOp A B := by
  ext X
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨Y, Z, f, g, h, hT, hY, hZ⟩
    exact ⟨Triangle.mk f g h, hT, hY, hZ, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨T, hT, h₁, h₃, ⟨e⟩⟩
    exact ObjectProperty.prop_of_iso _ e ⟨T.obj₁, T.obj₃, T.mor₁, T.mor₂, T.mor₃, hT, h₁, h₃⟩

/-! ### `⟨E⟩` as a property of objects -/

/-- The subcategory `⟨E⟩ = `[`Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.gen`] of [Stacks, Tag 09SI], read as
a property of objects of `D`. -/
def genProp (E : D) : ObjectProperty D := fun X => X ∈ gen E

omit [IsTriangulated D] in
/-- An object satisfies `genProp E` exactly when it lies in `gen E`. -/
@[simp]
theorem genProp_iff (E X : D) : genProp E X ↔ X ∈ gen E := Iff.rfl

omit [IsTriangulated D] in
private theorem genN_eq_retractClosure_extensionProductIter (E : D) (n : ℕ) :
    (fun X => X ∈ genN E n) =
      ObjectProperty.retractClosure
        (ObjectProperty.extensionProductIter (fun X => X ∈ add (shiftCat E)) n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    rw [ObjectProperty.extensionProductIter_zero, retractClosure_eq_smd]
    rfl
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [ObjectProperty.extensionProductIter_succ]
    show (fun X => X ∈ smd (starOp (gen₁ E) (genN E n))) = _
    rw [← retractClosure_eq_smd, ← extensionProduct_eq_star, ih]
    show ObjectProperty.retractClosure (ObjectProperty.extensionProduct
      (fun X => X ∈ smd (add (shiftCat E))) _) = _
    rw [← retractClosure_eq_smd,
      ObjectProperty.retractClosure_extensionProduct_retractClosure_retractClosure]

omit [IsTriangulated D] in
private theorem mem_genN_iff (E : D) (n : ℕ) (X : D) :
    X ∈ genN E n ↔ ObjectProperty.retractClosure
      (ObjectProperty.extensionProductIter (fun Y => Y ∈ add (shiftCat E)) n) X :=
  Iff.of_eq (congrFun (genN_eq_retractClosure_extensionProductIter E n) X)

/-- `⟨E⟩` is stable under retracts. -/
instance isStableUnderRetracts_genProp (E : D) : (genProp E).IsStableUnderRetracts where
  of_retract := by
    intro X Y r hY
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 hY
    refine Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨n, ?_⟩
    rw [mem_genN_iff] at hn ⊢
    exact ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderRetracts.of_retract r hn

/-- `⟨E⟩` is nonempty: it contains `E⟦0⟧`. -/
instance nonempty_genProp (E : D) : (genProp E).Nonempty :=
  ObjectProperty.nonempty_of_prop (X := (shiftFunctor D 0).obj E) (shift_mem_gen E 0)

omit [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated D] [IsTriangulated D] [HasFiniteBiproducts D] in
private theorem shift_mem_shiftCat_of_mem {E X : D} (k : ℤ) (hX : X ∈ shiftCat E) :
    (shiftFunctor D k).obj X ∈ shiftCat E := by
  obtain ⟨m, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hX
  exact ⟨m + k, ⟨(shiftFunctor D k).mapIso e ≪≫ ((shiftFunctorAdd' D m k (m + k) rfl).app E).symm⟩⟩

omit [HasZeroObject D] [Pretriangulated D] [IsTriangulated D] in
private theorem shift_mem_add_of_mem {A : Set D}
    (hA : ∀ (k : ℤ) (X : D), X ∈ A → (shiftFunctor D k).obj X ∈ A) (k : ℤ) {X : D}
    (hX : X ∈ add A) : (shiftFunctor D k).obj X ∈ add A := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hf, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hX
  exact ⟨r, (shiftFunctor D k).obj ∘ f, fun i => hA k _ (hf i),
    ⟨(shiftFunctor D k).mapIso e ≪≫ (shiftFunctor D k).mapBiproduct f⟩⟩

omit [HasZeroObject D] [Pretriangulated D] [IsTriangulated D] in
private theorem isStableUnderShift_add_shiftCat (E : D) :
    ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderShift (fun X => X ∈ add (shiftCat E)) ℤ where
  isStableUnderShiftBy k :=
    { le_shift := fun _ hX =>
        shift_mem_add_of_mem (fun k _ h => shift_mem_shiftCat_of_mem k h) k hX }

/-- `⟨E⟩` is stable under all shifts `X ↦ X⟦k⟧`, `k : ℤ`. -/
instance isStableUnderShift_genProp (E : D) : (genProp E).IsStableUnderShift ℤ where
  isStableUnderShiftBy k :=
    { le_shift := by
        have := isStableUnderShift_add_shiftCat E
        intro X hX
        obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 hX
        refine Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨n, ?_⟩
        rw [mem_genN_iff] at hn ⊢
        exact ObjectProperty.le_shift _ k _ hn }

/-- `⟨E⟩` is closed under extensions: if `X ⟶ Y ⟶ Z ⟶ X⟦1⟧` is distinguished and `X`, `Z` lie
in `⟨E⟩`, then so does `Y`. -/
instance isTriangulatedClosed₂_genProp (E : D) : (genProp E).IsTriangulatedClosed₂ := by
  apply ObjectProperty.IsTriangulatedClosed₂.mk'
  intro T hT h₁ h₃
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 h₁
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 h₃
  rw [mem_genN_iff] at hn hm
  refine Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨n + (m + 1), ?_⟩
  rw [mem_genN_iff, ObjectProperty.extensionProductIter_add' _ rfl]
  exact ObjectProperty.extensionProduct_retractClosure_retractClosure_le _ _ _
    ⟨T.obj₁, T.obj₃, T.mor₁, T.mor₂, T.mor₃, hT, hn, hm⟩

/-- **`⟨E⟩` is a triangulated subcategory of `D`.** It contains a zero object, is stable under
all shifts and is closed under extensions; together with stability under retracts this is the
content of [Stacks, Tag 0ATG] for `⟨E⟩`. -/
instance isTriangulated_genProp (E : D) : (genProp E).IsTriangulated where

/-! ### Membership in `⟨E⟩` -/

omit [IsTriangulated D] in
/-- `⟨E⟩` is closed under isomorphisms. -/
theorem mem_gen_of_iso {E X Y : D} (e : X ≅ Y) (hX : X ∈ gen E) : Y ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.prop_of_iso (genProp E) e hX

omit [IsTriangulated D] in
/-- `⟨E⟩` is stable under shifts: if `X ∈ ⟨E⟩` then `X⟦k⟧ ∈ ⟨E⟩` for every `k : ℤ`. -/
theorem shift_mem_gen_of_mem {E X : D} (k : ℤ) (hX : X ∈ gen E) :
    (shiftFunctor D k).obj X ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.le_shift (genProp E) k X hX

/-- **`⟨E⟩` is closed under extensions.** -/
theorem mem_gen₂_of_distTriang {E : D} (T : Triangle D) (hT : T ∈ distTriang D)
    (h₁ : T.obj₁ ∈ gen E) (h₃ : T.obj₃ ∈ gen E) : T.obj₂ ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₂ (genProp E) T hT h₁ h₃

/-- **`⟨E⟩` is closed under cones.** -/
theorem mem_gen₃_of_distTriang {E : D} (T : Triangle D) (hT : T ∈ distTriang D)
    (h₁ : T.obj₁ ∈ gen E) (h₂ : T.obj₂ ∈ gen E) : T.obj₃ ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₃ (genProp E) T hT h₁ h₂

/-- **`⟨E⟩` is closed under fibres.** -/
theorem mem_gen₁_of_distTriang {E : D} (T : Triangle D) (hT : T ∈ distTriang D)
    (h₂ : T.obj₂ ∈ gen E) (h₃ : T.obj₃ ∈ gen E) : T.obj₁ ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₁ (genProp E) T hT h₂ h₃

/-- **A finite tower of extensions of objects of `⟨E⟩` lies in `⟨E⟩`.** The specialization of
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_triangleChain` to the subcategory `⟨E⟩` generated by an
object `E`. -/
theorem mem_gen_of_triangleChain (E : D) {Y B : ℕ → D} (N : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ i < N, ∃ (f : Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1)) (g : Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i) (h : B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang D)
    (hY : Y 0 ∈ gen E) (hB : ∀ i < N, B i ∈ gen E) : Y N ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.prop_of_triangleChain (genProp E) N hT hY hB

/-- **A finite tower whose bottom is a zero object.** `mem_gen_of_triangleChain` with `Y 0` only
assumed to be a zero object; see `mem_gen_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration` for the same statement
indexed the way the stupid filtration of an acyclic complex produces it. -/
theorem mem_gen_of_isZero_triangleChain (E : D) {Y B : ℕ → D} (N : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ i < N, ∃ (f : Y i ⟶ Y (i + 1)) (g : Y (i + 1) ⟶ B i) (h : B i ⟶ (Y i)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang D)
    (hY : IsZero (Y 0)) (hB : ∀ i < N, B i ∈ gen E) : Y N ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_triangleChain (genProp E) N hT hY hB

/-- **The initial term of a bounded acyclic complex lies in `⟨E⟩` as soon as the other terms
do.** This is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration` for `⟨E⟩`: with
`U p` the stupid truncation `σ^{≤p}` of an acyclic complex `0 ⟶ A 0 ⟶ ⋯ ⟶ A M ⟶ 0` and `B p` a
shift of its `p`-th term, the hypotheses are that the whole complex `U M` is zero and that
`B 1, …, B M` lie in `⟨E⟩`, and the conclusion is that the initial term `U 0 = A 0` does.

Since `⟨E⟩` is stable under shifts (`Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.shift_mem_gen_of_mem`), the
hypothesis `hB` is implied by `A p ∈ ⟨E⟩` for `1 ≤ p ≤ M`. -/
theorem mem_gen_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration (E : D) {U B : ℕ → D} (M : ℕ)
    (hT : ∀ p, 0 < p → p ≤ M → ∃ (f : U p ⟶ U (p - 1)) (g : U (p - 1) ⟶ B p)
      (h : B p ⟶ (U p)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧), Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang D)
    (hU : IsZero (U M)) (hB : ∀ p, 0 < p → p ≤ M → B p ∈ gen E) : U 0 ∈ gen E :=
  ObjectProperty.prop_of_isZero_of_stupidFiltration (genProp E) M hT hU hB

end Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators

end
